### Production URL

A Worker's public URL is read by {{#if (hasLibrary "better-auth")}}`BETTER_AUTH_URL`, a secret a deploy fails without{{/if}}{{#if (and (hasLibrary "better-auth") (and (hasLibrary "trpc") (has "stack" "nextjs")))}} and by {{/if}}{{#if appUrlReader}}`NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL`, which Next.js freezes into the build and {{appUrlReader}}{{else if (and (hasLibrary "trpc") (has "stack" "nextjs"))}}`NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL`, which Next.js freezes into the build and the server-side tRPC client calls{{/if}}, yet `wrangler deploy` is the first command that prints it. Learn it before the first build and deploy, from the Cloudflare account:

1. Find the account id (the `Account ID` column; with several accounts, take the one you deploy to):

   ```bash
   {{#inDirectory "apps" (deployAppDir)}}{{installedBinaryRunner}} wrangler whoami{{/inDirectory}}
   ```

2. Ask the Workers API for the `workers.dev` subdomain of that account, with the token of the Wrangler login (or `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`). The token goes through a pipe, so it never appears in the command line of `curl`; `WRANGLER_HIDE_BANNER` keeps Wrangler's banner out of it:

   ```bash
   {{#inDirectory "apps" (deployAppDir)}}WRANGLER_HIDE_BANNER=true {{installedBinaryRunner}} wrangler auth token{{/inDirectory}} | sed 's/^/Authorization: Bearer /' | curl -s -H @- https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/<account id>/workers/subdomain
   ```

   The answer holds `"subdomain": "<subdomain>"` under `result`. An error with code `10007` instead means the account has no `workers.dev` subdomain yet: register one at `https://dash.cloudflare.com/<account id>/workers/onboarding`, then ask again.

The URL of a Worker is then `https://<worker name>.<subdomain>.workers.dev`, its name being the `name` of its `wrangler.jsonc`:
{{#each apps}}
{{#if (or (appSecrets) (eq stackName "nextjs"))}}

- {{#if (isMono)}}`{{appName}}`: {{/if}}`https://{{> cloudflare/worker-name projectName=@root.projectName}}.<subdomain>.workers.dev`
{{/if}}
{{/each}}

A Worker served from a custom domain or a route uses that URL instead.
{{#if (or appUrlReader (and (hasLibrary "trpc") (has "stack" "nextjs")))}}

Build with it: `export NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=<the URL>` in the shell of the build, before the build command, so `.env` needs no production value.{{#if (hasLibrary "better-auth")}} `BETTER_AUTH_URL` is the same URL, set with the other secrets.{{/if}}
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
